{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 41, :comments ["<b>This is to me twenty years in your house.</b> And above he said, ״זֶה עֶשְׂרִים שָׁנָה אָנֹכִי עִמָּךְ״, and he did not mention the word ״לִי״; also he said ״עִמָּךְ״ in place of ״בְּבֵיתֶךָ״. For in truth Jacob was not in Laban's house except for one month, as it says, ״וַיֵּשֶׁב עִמּוֹ חֹדֶשׁ יָמִים״ (Genesis 29:14) — meaning that only for a month of days did he dwell with him in his house; but during all the rest of the times he was sojourning in the fields and tents to tend Laban's flocks, and was not in Laban's house, as he said, ״הָיִיתִי בַיּוֹם אֲכָלַנִי חֹרֶב וְקֶרַח בַּלָּיְלָה״ (Genesis 31:40). Therefore he said, ״זֶה עֶשְׂרִים שָׁנָה אָנֹכִי עִמָּךְ״ — but not in your house. And in any event, even this month of days that he dwelt in the house of the wicked man and the deceiver did not seem in his eyes like a few days, but like a long time, because they were days of distress to him, which appear as many days. And he said, ״אוֹיָה לִי כִּי גַרְתִּי מֶשֶׁךְ״ (Psalms 120:5) — a long time with the wicked man, and even if it was little, ״לִי״ — meaning, in my eyes it is weighed as though I had been all twenty years in his house. Therefore he said, ״זֶה לִּי עֶשְׂרִים שָׁנָה בְּבֵיתֶךָ״ — in truth they are not twenty years but only one month alone, but to me this month is weighed as twenty years, not as my mother said, ״וְיָשַׁבְתָּ עִמּוֹ יָמִים אֲחָדִים״ (Genesis 27:44) — for perhaps my mother did not know the greatness of his wickedness, but my heart knows the bitterness of his soul: how much distress I suffered from being with you in your house itself." "Another matter: at first Jacob mentioned all that he himself did with him — how he acted with him in faithfulness — and afterward he mentioned all that Laban did to him. Therefore he said first, ״זֶה עֶשְׂרִים שָׁנָה אָנֹכִי עִמָּךְ״ (Genesis 31:38), meaning: I acted with you in faithfulness, ״טְרֵפָה לֹא הֵבֵאתִי אֵלֶיךָ״ and so on (Genesis 31:39). And this entire account all speaks of Jacob's faithfulness. And afterward he said to him: See, in contrast to this, what you did to me. And he said, ״זֶה לִּי עֶשְׂרִים שָׁנָה בְּבֵיתֶךָ״ (Genesis 31:38) — see what you did to me: behold, I served you fourteen years for your two daughters and six years for your flocks, and despite all this, ״וַתַּחֲלֵף אֶת מַשְׂכֻּרְתִּי עֲשֶׂרֶת מֹנִים״ (Genesis 31:41), and not according to the recompense of my hands did you act toward me. And through this the distinction is well settled — that at first he mentioned ״עִמָּךְ״, and afterward said ״זֶה לִּי״ — and it is a precious interpretation."], :book :genesis, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {1 "Both comment 0 and comment 1 cite Genesis 31:38 for the phrase ״זֶה לִּי עֶשְׂרִים שָׁנָה בְּבֵיתֶךָ״; the verse address is carried over as written, though the lemma head at the top of comment 0 cites no verse number."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:31:32.923329605Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}